===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|en|id=on|inh|enm>at>on|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|at}}, from {{inh|en|ang|æt||at, near, by, toward}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*at||at, near, to}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*h₂éd||near, at}}. Cognate with {{cog|sco|at||at}}, {{cog|frr|äät}}, {{m|frr|äit}}, {{m|frr|et}}, {{m|frr|it||at}}, {{cog|da|at||to}}, {{cog|sv|åt||for, toward}}, {{cog|no|åt||to}}, {{cog|fo|at||at, to, toward}}, {{cog|is|að||to, towards}}, {{cog|got|𐌰𐍄||at}}, {{cog|la|ad||to, near}}.

====Preposition====
{{en-prep}}

# [[in|In]], [[near]], or in the general vicinity of a particular [[place]].
#: {{ux|en|Caesar was '''at''' Rome.}}
#: {{co|en|'''at''' the corner of Fourth Street and Vine}}
#: {{co|en|'''at''' Jim’s house}}
#* '''1919''', Plutarch, [http://penelope.uchicago.edu/Thayer/E/Roman/Texts/Plutarch/Lives/Cicero*.html “The Life of Cicero”] in ''Parallel Lives'', 43 (Bernadotte Perrin, trans.):
#*: Hirtius and Pansa, who were good men and admirers of Cicero, begged him not to desert them, and undertook to put down Antony if Cicero would remain '''at''' Rome.
#* {{RQ:Schuster Hepaticae|volume=V|page=4|text=(''b'') sporophyte with foot reduced, the entire sporophyte enveloped by the calyptra, which is ± stipitate '''at''' the base.}}
#* '''2016''', [https://web.archive.org/web/20170930001420/https://learningenglish.voanews.com/a/lets-learn-english-lesson-5-where-are-you/3168971.html VOA Learning English] (public domain):
#*: Today my friend Marsha is '''at''' her friend’s house.
#*:: {{audio|en|Today my friend Marsha is at her friend's house.ogg|a=US}}
# {{qualifier|indicating time}} {{n-g|Indicating occurrence in an instant of time or a period of time relatively short in context or from the speaker’s perspective.}}
#: {{co|en|'''at''' six o’clock}}
#: {{co|en|'''at''' closing time}}
#: {{co|en|'''at''' night}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1838|title=The Family Magazine| passage=Lafayette was major-general in the American army '''at''' the age of 18 {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=April 19, 2012|author=Josh Halliday|work=the Guardian| title=[http://www.guardian.co.uk/technology/2012/apr/19/free-speech-haven-lawless-cesspool Free speech haven or lawless cesspool – can the internet be civilised?]| passage=Other global taboos, such as sex and suicide, manifest themselves widely online, with websites offering suicide guides and Hot XXX Action seconds away '''at''' the click of a button. The UK government will come under pressure to block access to pornographic websites this year when a committee of MPs publishes its report on protecting children online.}}
#* '''2016''', [https://web.archive.org/web/20171030003034/https://learningenglish.voanews.com/a/lets-learn-english-lesson-8-are-you-busy/3253185.html VOA Learning English] (public domain)
#*: Hi, Anne. Are you busy? &mdash; Hi, Anna. Yes. '''At''' 10 a.m. I am writing.
#*:: {{audio|en|Hi, Anne. Are you busy - Hi, Anna. Yes. At 10 a.m. I am writing.ogg|a=US}}
# In the [[direction#Noun|direction]] of ({{n-g|often implied to be in a [[hostile]] or [[careless]] manner}}).
#: {{ux|en|Don’t just [[talk at|talk '''at''']] someone; really listen to what they have to say.}}
#: {{ux|en|He threw the ball '''at''' me.}}
#: {{ux|en|He shouted '''at''' her.}}
#* {{RQ:Ferguson Zollenstein|IV| passage=“My Continental prominence is improving,” I commented dryly. <br> Von Lindowe cut '''at''' a furze bush with his silver-mounted rattan. <br> “Quite so,” he said as dryly, his hand at his mustache. “I may say if your intentions were known your life would not be worth a curse.”}}
#* {{quote-av|en|title=[[w:Barbie (film)|Barbie]]|actor=w:Ryan Gosling|role=[[w:Ken (doll)|Ken]]|date=9 July 2023|text=Come on in. I’ll play the guitar '''at''' you.}}
# {{senseid|en|price}} {{n-g|Denotes a price.}}
#: {{ux|en|3 apples '''at''' 2¢ (each)}}
#: {{ux|en|The offer was '''at''' $30,000 before negotiations.}}
# [[occupy|Occupied]] in (activity).
#: {{co|en|men '''at''' work}}
# In a state of.
#: {{ux|en|She is [[at sixes and sevens|'''at''' sixes and sevens]] with him.}}
#: {{ux|en|They are [[at loggerheads|'''at''' loggerheads]] over how best to tackle the fiscal cliff.}}
#: {{ux|en|The city was [[at the mercy of|'''at''' the mercy of]] the occupying forces.}}
# {{non-gloss definition|Indicates a position on a scale or in a series.}}
#: {{ux|en|Sell '''at''' 90.}}
#: {{ux|en|Tiger finished the round '''at''' tenth, seven strokes behind the leaders.}}
#: {{ux|en|I’m offering it—just to select customers—[[at cost|'''at''' cost]].}}
# Because of.
#: {{co|en|to laugh '''at''' a joke}}
#: {{co|en|mad '''at''' their comments}}
# {{n-g|Indicates a means, method, or manner.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1995|author=Richard Klein|title=Cigarettes are Sublime|isbn=0822316412|page=41|passage={{...}} to be sold '''at''' auction for sixty gold francs.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=Sami Moubayed|title=Syria and the USA: Washington's Relations with Damascus|isbn=0857730673|passage=A few days later, on 1 October, King Hussein opened the Jordanian Parliament by speaking '''at''' length about the crisis in Syria,}}
# Holding a given [[speed]] or [[rate#English|rate]].
#: {{ux|en|It is growing '''at''' the rate of 3% a year.}}
#: {{ux|en|Cruising along '''at''' fifty miles per hour.}}
# {{lb|en|used for skills (including in activities) or areas of knowledge}} On the [[subject]] of; [[regarding]].
#: {{ux|en|The twins were both bad '''at''' chemistry.}}
#: {{ux|en|He slipped '''at''' marksmanship over his extended vacation.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2015|title=Sanyan Stories: Favorites from a Ming Dynasty Collection|page=157|isbn=0295805692
|passage=She’s good '''at''' playing musical instruments, singing and dancing, chess, calligraphy, and painting.}}
# {{lb|en|Ireland|stressed pronunciation}} Bothering, irritating, causing discomfort to
#* '''1995''' Keith Wood, quoted in David Hughes, "[http://www.independent.co.uk/sport/rugby-union-wood-oddson-to-take-one-against-the-head-1568622.html Wood odds-on to take one against the head]", in ''The Independent'' (London) 18 January:
#*: I think ‘Jesus, my back is '''at''' me’. Then I get the ball. Off you go for 10 yards and you don’t feel a thing. Then you stop and think: ‘Jesus, it’s '''at''' me again’[.]
#* '''2014''' Marian Keyes "[https://web.archive.org/web/20140203045758/http://www.mariankeyes.com/newsletter/January2014-2?forumboardid=26&forumtopicid=26 Antarctic Diary - Part 2]" personal website (January 2014):
#*: He seems to be saying. “Ah, go on, you’re making the other lads feel bad.” But the 4th fella says, “No. Don’t be '''‘at’''' me. I’m just not in the form right now, I’ll stay where I am, thanks.”
# {{lb|en|UK|Commonwealth|Ireland|especially finance}} {{q|also '''as at'''; before dates}} On a particular date.
#* '''n.d.''', quoted in ''Longmans Business Dictionary'':
#*: balance '''as at''' 20th March 1999

=====Usage notes=====
* ''He threw the ball to me'' &mdash; (so I could catch it).
* ''He threw the ball at me'' &mdash; (trying to hit me with it).

* ''He talked to her'' &mdash; (conversationally).
* ''He shouted at her'' &mdash; (aggressively).

