|passage=Knud hørte, '''at''' bedstefaren lagde værktøjet fra sig
|translation=Knud heard '''that''' his grandfather put down the tool.}}
#* {{quote-book|da|year=1876|author=J.P. Jacobsen|title=Fru Marie Grubbe|volume=1|page=67|url=https://books.google.dk/books?id=VdK9DgAAQBAJ&pg=PT59
|passage=Hun var overbevist om '''at''' det var sandt.
|translation=She was convinced '''that''' it was true.}}
# {{lb|da|archaic}} [[that]], [[in order that]], [[so that]] {{q|introduces an {{glossary|adverbial clause}} stating the purpose}}
#* '''1856''', Christian Winther, ''Hr. Peder Jernskjæg'', from ''Hjortens Flugt'' / https://kalliope.org/da/text/winther2018100610:
#*: Og Hjorten vil jeg fange, | At Korset jeg kan faae.
#*:: And the deer, I will catch, that I may win the cross.
#* {{quote-text|da|year=1987|author=Thomas Bruun|title=Et paradisisk blik. Humoresker og grotesker
|passage=det er helvedes svært, '''at''' du bare ved det.
|translation=it is damned difficult, just '''that''' you know it.}}
#: {{synonyms|da|for at}}
# [[that]], [[so that]] {{q|introduces an {{glossary|adverbial clause}} stating the result, normally after a demonstrative adverb or pronoun}}
#* {{quote-text|da|year=1902|author=Karin Michaëlis|title=Barnet|url=https://books.google.dk/books?id=A_4kDgAAQBAJ&pg=PT62
|passage=Jeg er saa fattig, '''at''' jeg sulter paa Sjæl og Legeme.
|translation=I am so poor '''that''' I starve in my soul and my body.}}
